.TH FALSE 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
false \- provide an unsuccessful truth value
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B false
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I False
does nothing, unsuccessfully.
It provides a false condition to
.IR sh (1).
For example:
.PP
.B false || echo failed
.SH FILES
/usr/man/FALSE  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
true(1), sh(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 1.
